; Janax's living desktop (Capitan: "the loop has life: it always explores, but it is never the repetition of the same").
; Every piece of the screen is a cloud of particles: Razar's window, Luma's window, the taskbar (10428 particles).
; Each particle has its home cell in its piece, a position and a speed (x256), and a spring to its home:
;   v += k*(home - p) >> 8;  v -= v*40 >> 8;  p += v      (k = 20: a period of ~22 frames; damping ratio ~0.28)
; Each frame the cloud (.nube v3, one level, 160x100, every cell set) is rebuilt and shown (request 40); between
; frames Janax waits for an event (request 41): 33 ms while anything moves, for ever when everything rests.
; - A title bar dragged moves its window; near the grab point the springs are stiffer, so it stretches like jelly.
; - A close button: the window flies apart. The start button: the closed windows fly back. A little tower: a kick.
;   A click on a window brings it to the front.
; - Nobody doing anything: Razar explores its own body, one small push at a time, among the 96 combinations of
;   piece (6) x push (shove, pulse, twist, shear) x direction/strength (4) it has not tried in this round;
;   a seeded generator picks among the untried ones, so it never repeats one. When all are tried it rests and waits
;   for ever (nothing is spent). Any click opens a new round: the table of the tried ones is cleared.
; Ends when the window is closed: j0 = the frames drawn. Generated by gen_vivo.py.
; Room 0: 100h the queue, 140h the event, 200h the variables, 400h the pieces, 600h the parts, 800h the tried ones,
; 1004h the cloud (28 + 2000 + 48000 bytes), 10000h the particles (64 bytes each).
include '../../escalon0/janax.inc'
jfirst j1, 100000h
jldi j14, 0                     ; j14 stays 0: the variables live below 8000h
; ---- the cloud's header and its cells, once
  jldi j1, 01004h
  jldi j2, 04Eh
  jstb j2, j1, 0
  jldi j2, 055h
  jstb j2, j1, 1
